;; posix's spawning without fork (PY6e; Modules/posixmodule.c's os_posix_spawn_impl and os_spawnv_impl): the
;; child started by Go's ForkExec, the only way a multithreaded Go process starts one. posix_spawn's file actions
;; are carried out in the parent as the descriptor table the child gets (ForkExec's Files: an open's descriptor
;; opened here, a close -1, a dup2 the source's entry), every other descriptor inherited unless close-on-exec, as
;; posix_spawn(3) leaves them. setsigmask and setsigdef (queue 231) are applied around ForkExec, which takes no signal
;; sets: the child gets the forking thread's mask (Go's BeforeFork saves it, the child restores it), so the mask is set
;; on that thread, locked to the goroutine, for the fork alone; and Go's child resets every signal Go handles to
;; SIG_DFL but keeps an ignored one, so a setsigdef signal the process ignores is handled by Go (notified to a channel
;; nobody reads, which drops it as SIG_IGN would) for the fork alone. spawnv and its kin (P_WAIT, P_NOWAIT) are the native ones os.py takes in place of its fork-based
;; _spawnvef; a program that cannot be executed is the child's exit status 127, as _spawnvef's child exits.



